{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you trusted in your evil, etc.</b> And your knowledge: a hint to external wisdom that suppresses [recognition of] the Name." "And the alef of <b>ro'eni</b> is contracted with kamatz because it is guttural." "<b>Your wisdom.</b> Which you thought was wisdom." "<b>Your stubbornness.</b> An epithet for prevailing, and for not wanting to turn back from his way." "<b>And I am.</b> Like its parallel: \"I am wisdom, and there is no wise man besides me.\""], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:25.453520930Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}